son":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110421","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110421","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110421.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110421.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"I noticed that the `is_selected` method on `EditorNode3DGizmo`  is not properly exposed in GDScript. This function is important to be able to make proper gizmo plugins that only show when the node is selected.\n\nThis PR aims to fix this by exposing `is_selected` in GDScript. I didn't add bindings for `set_selected` as I assumed it is only used internally and cannot be successfully called from user code. But I could add bindings for that function as well if needed.\n\nI'm interested to know if there are any way to workaround this issue for current versions of Godot (`4.4.1` or `4.5-rc2`).","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110421/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110421/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}